  {
   "k": "sj3n6r",
   "en": "Ethiopia in By Blood Alone is a country that gets exiled when invaded by ⟦0⟧, even if it not belongs to any faction. You can choose a host country as a triggered event, and you get exiled when you lose the war. Said events are in the Italian-Ethiopian war events, and are several and complex. The on-actions of ⟦1⟧ contain the following code as an ⟦2⟧ effect: ⟦3⟧ This code is simple enough. ⟦4⟧ is a variable containing a dynamic tag, which defines the country in which ⟦5⟧ has permission to get exiled in. Yet, this code in a custom event or decision doesn't really change anything as a player, as you still play in your original country if it wasn't annexed.",
